ng a number of  in-person supports to families including  actually uh device repair online  learning support  um mental health resources actually we  are offering covent testing  um  to support families and so  to help make that not be continue to be  an issue  in the early stages of this work um when  i was out in neighborhoods  in some ways uh families just didn't  feel like they  had the  all of the clear communication and  information about what was available to  them what they were supposed to do how  they were to participate  um and so that's why the home visits  were so important because it really  helped us face to face describe to  someone what to do get their cell phone  number  and just solve the problem alongside of  them  we also have we also launched an online  learning help hotline we've had over 000  calls to date um  there so that families can continue to  call in and say  gosh i need help this isn't working i  don't know what to do how do i enroll  now that you know so much is so  different  um so those are a few of the reasons  that families shared with us and and  some of the things that we've done  to try to support them and address that  so it sounds like it's you know in some  categories just tech difficulties  and then probably a little bit of an  activation energy of just not knowing  how to engage in this in this new  this new world on the other issue you  mentioned the the students failing  disproportionately especially at the  high school level how do y'all  categorize that how much of that is the  access issue we just talked about how  much of that is uh kind of stress and  mental health and anxiety and depression  and how much of that is just something  something else  yeah  so we're actually studying the  relationship right now um between  student performance and attendance to  see  um you know what the  relationship is there  we've also  been actively engaging in focus groups  with our students to hear from them you  know  what their 